# Frontend / UX Review: agents-arwaky CLI & Terminal UI

## Summary

This review covers the **terminal-facing UI/UX layer** of the agents-arwaky orchestrator — the primary user-facing surfaces being the `aa` CLI (`tools/cli/arwaky.py`), shared terminal output helpers (`tools/lib/ui.py`), shell completion (`tools/completion/completion.py`), and the skill/connect managers. Since agents-arwaky is a CLI-first tool (no web GUI), the review adapts frontend heuristics to terminal UX: color accessibility, output formatting, error handling, confirmation flows, and visual consistency.

---

## Findings

### Accessibility (a11y)

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| 1 | 🔴 CRITICAL | Status conveyed by **color alone** (green ✓ / red ✗ / yellow ⚠). Colorblind users (8% of males) cannot distinguish states if symbols fail to render. | `tools/lib/ui.py` lines `ok()`, `warn()`, `err()` | Always pair color with a distinct **text label** prefix: `[OK]`, `[WARN]`, `[FAIL]` alongside symbols. |
| 2 | 🟡 WARNING | Unicode symbols `✓ ⚠ ✗ ↳` used throughout. These fail on Windows `cmd.exe`, older terminals, and some SSH sessions, producing mojibake. | `ui.py`, `skill.py`, `connect.py`, `arwaky.py` | Detect encoding support: `if sys.stdout.encoding != 'utf-8': fallback to ASCII` (`[OK]`, `[!]`, `[X]`). |
| 3 | 🟡 WARNING | No `--plain` / `--no-color` CLI flag. Only respects `NO_COLOR` env var. Users piping output or using screen readers must set an env var. | `ui.py` `_color_enabled()` | Add global `--plain` flag to `arwaky.py` that sets `os.environ["NO_COLOR"]="1"` before importing `ui`. |
| 4 | 🟡 WARNING | ANSI escape sequences injected into log lines are **noise for screen readers** (NVDA, VoiceOver read literal `\033[0;32m`). | `ui.py` all color constants | When `NO_COLOR` is set, also strip symbols to plain ASCII labels. |
| 5 | 🟢 INFO | No `--json` structured output option for machine-consumable results (accessibility for automation users). | `arwaky.py` all commands | Add `--json` flag to `status`, `list`, `doctor` for screen-reader-friendly / parseable output. |

### Responsiveness & Layout

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| 6 | 🔴 CRITICAL | `cmd_status` uses `f"{tool.id:<14} {cat_color}{tool.category:<10}{RESET} ..."` — **ANSI escape codes inflate the padding width**, causing misaligned columns in every row with color. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_status()` | Strip ANSI when computing width: `visible = re.sub(r'\033\[[0-9;]*m', '', text)` then pad based on `len(visible)`. |
| 7 | 🟡 WARNING | Banner ASCII art is hardcoded 42-char wide. Breaks visually on terminals < 50 columns. | `ui.py` `banner()` | Wrap banner print in `if shutil.get_terminal_size().columns >= 50:` else print short text version. |
| 8 | 🟡 WARNING | `cmd_list` table uses fixed `<45` for description. Long descriptions truncate silently with no ellipsis. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_list()` | Use `textwrap.shorten(desc, width=45, placeholder="…")`. |
| 9 | 🟢 INFO | No dynamic column sizing based on `shutil.get_terminal_size()`. | `arwaky.py` | Compute column widths from terminal size minus padding. |

### UX Patterns & User Flow

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| 10 | 🔴 CRITICAL | `cmd_install` with no args installs **all tools** without confirmation. Destructive disk/network operation triggered by bare `aa install`. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_install()` | Add confirmation: `if target == "all": confirm = input("Install ALL tools? [y/N] ")`. |
| 11 | 🔴 CRITICAL | `cmd_uninstall --all` removes all binaries/data with **no confirmation prompt** (unlike `cmd_reset` which requires typing "RESET"). | `arwaky.py` `cmd_uninstall()` | Add same "RESET"-style confirmation or at minimum `--yes` flag requirement. |
| 12 | 🟡 WARNING | `cmd_reset` requires typing "RESET" but does not show what will be destroyed before the prompt. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_reset()` | List affected paths (binaries, data dirs, configs) **before** the confirmation prompt. |
| 13 | 🟡 WARNING | No progress indicator during `cmd_install` builds (Rust compile can take minutes). User sees no feedback between tool installs. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_install()` loop | Add `info(f"Installing {tool.id} ({i}/{len(tools)})...")` counter. |
| 14 | 🟡 WARNING | `cmd_run` error for missing binary suggests `aa install {tool.id}` but doesn't offer to run it. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_run()` | Offer interactive: `Install now? [y/N]` then `exec cmd_install([tool.id])`. |
| 15 | 🟡 WARNING | `cmd_check` error count uses `errors` variable but always exits 0 if JSON/py passes — doesn't propagate shellcheck warnings. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_check()` | Track warnings separately and display summary. |
| 16 | 🟢 INFO | `cmd_help` doesn't show examples. New users get a command list but no usage patterns. | `arwaky.py` `cmd_help()` | Add 3-4 common examples at the bottom. |
| 17 | 🟢 INFO | No `--version` flag on `aa` CLI. | `arwaky.py` `main()` dispatch | Add `"version": lambda a: print("agents-arwaky v1.0.0")` to dispatch. |

### Component Quality

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| 18 | 🟡 WARNING | `ui.py` color init is inconsistent: `BOLD = _c("1")`, `DIM = _c("2")` but colors use `_c("0;32m")` — mixed SGR formats. | `ui.py` lines 8-15 | Normalize: `BOLD = _c("1m")`, `DIM = _c("2m")` (add `m` suffix consistently). |
| 19 | 🟡 WARNING | `_ENABLED` in `ui.py` is evaluated at **import time** via `_color_enabled()`. If stdout is later redirected (e.g., piping to `jq`), colors persist incorrectly. | `ui.py` line 5 | Make `_ENABLED` a lazy property or re-check in `_c()`: `if not _color_enabled(): return ""`. |
| 20 | 🟡 WARNING | `load_tools()` in `manifest.py` re-reads and re-parses `manifest.json` on **every call**. Called multiple times per CLI invocation. | `manifest.py` `load_tools()` | Cache with `functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1)` or module-level `_cache`. |
| 21 | 🟡 WARNING | `install_node_tool` shared utility exists but 4 installers (`install_blender.py`, `install_mnemosyne.py`, etc.) still duplicate launcher-writing logic inline instead of using `utility_launcher_writer.py`. | `tools/install/install_blender.py` et al. | Refactor to call `write_uv_launchers()` from `utility_launcher_writer.py`. |
| 22 | 🟢 INFO | `completion.py` generates only bash-style completion (`complete -F`) but claims zsh support. Zsh users get bash completion which works but misses zsh-native features (`compdef`, descriptions). | `completion.py` `generate_bash()` | Add `generate_zsh()` using `compdef` and `_describe`. |

### Visual Consistency & Design Tokens

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| 23 | 🟡 WARNING | **Inconsistent log prefixes** across the codebase: `==>` (ui.py), `>>>` (installers), `✓`/`✗` (skill.py), `↷` (skill.py skip), `[OK]`/`[WARN]` (gates.sh), `▸` (ci.sh). No unified design language. | Multiple files | Define a single log vocabulary in `ui.py`: `info` → `==>`, `ok` → `✓`, `warn` → `⚠`, `err` → `✗`. Use these everywhere; deprecate raw `print(">>>")`. |
| 24 | 🟡 WARNING | Some scripts use `ui.py` helpers (`info`, `ok`, `warn`) while others use raw `print(f"  ✓ ...")` — bypassing the color/accessibility layer. | `skill.py`, `connect.py`, installers | Replace all raw `print("  ✓")` with `ui.ok()`. |
| 25 | 🟢 INFO | No log-level control. All output goes to stdout at same verbosity. No `--verbose` / `--quiet` on most commands. | Global | Add `-v`/`-q` global flags routed through `ui.py` to suppress/show `sub()` messages. |

### Performance (Client-Side)

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | -------------- |
| 26 | 🟡 WARNING | `get_all_skill_files()` in `skill.py` scans entire `tools/skills/` directory with `rglob` on **every invocation** (called in list, install, uninstall, show). | `skill.py` | Cache result at module level; invalidate only if mtime changes. |
| 27 | 🟡 WARNING | `arwaky_server_names()` in `connect.py` spawns a **subprocess** (`engine.py`) every time it's called. Called once per file during disconnect. | `connect.py` | Cache the server names list once per process run. |
| 28 | 🟢 INFO | `cmd_status` iterates all tools and calls `executable_path()` (which does `shutil.which` + `Path.exists`) per tool. ~15 tools × 2 filesystem calls. | `arwaky.py` | Acceptable for 15 tools, but if tool count grows, batch-check `bin_home()` contents once. |

